# Development-only content — keep it out of the published UPM package.
# `npm pack` runs from this directory (see scripts/pack-release.sh), so these paths
# are relative to package/. Note: npm does NOT read the repo-root .gitignore when
# packing from here, so anything that must not ship has to be listed explicitly.

# Unit / integration tests (PlayMode + EditMode) are for repo development only and
# are not part of the shipped player.
Tests/
Tests.meta

# Test-generated sample art lives under Tests/Runtime/Resources and is gitignored at
# the repo root, but npm cannot see that — exclude it here too so a tarball packed
# locally (after the tests have run) never sweeps the sample assets in.
**/Resources/Ringo/

# Dev-only AddOn dispatch check. SpriteStudioAddOnCatalogBuilder already excludes the
# "TestStub" id from the generated catalog, so nothing in a shipped package references
# this shader; SpriteStudioAddOnRegistry.TryResolveShader folds to the default material
# when Shader.Find comes up empty. Keep it in the repo (the registry table still lists
# it for local dispatch checks), just don't publish it.
Runtime/Resources/Shaders/AddOns/SpriteStudioTestStub.shader
Runtime/Resources/Shaders/AddOns/SpriteStudioTestStub.shader.meta
